# ⛔ THIS BOX HAS `core.autocrlf=true` AND THIS REPO HAD NO ATTRIBUTES FILE, so
# git decided text-vs-binary by SNIFFING every blob. A font that ever sniffed as
# text would have every 0x0A rewritten to 0x0D 0x0A on checkout — a corrupt
# .woff2 that @font-face rejects SILENTLY, leaving the chart axis in a fallback
# face. That is the exact failure self-hosting the font was adopted to remove, so
# it is not left to a heuristic.
#
# (Sniffing does get it right today — `git diff --cached --numstat` reports `- -`
# for all four and the stored blobs are byte-identical to disk. This is here so
# that stays true for a font whose first 8 kB happens to contain no NUL.)
#
# The self-consistency rail is in tests/test_chart_parity_harness.py: a woff2
# header declares its own total length, and CRLF conversion breaks that equality.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

# ⛔⛔ PINE SOURCES ARE BYTE-FIDELITY ARTIFACTS AND THIS BOX REWRITES LINE
# ENDINGS ON CHECKOUT. Measured 2026-09-11:
# `tests/fixtures/member/uncharted-volume.pine` was 34,950 bytes on disk against a
# 34,342-byte blob — exactly its 608 CRLFs — so
# `test_the_file_on_disk_matches_BOTH_recorded_hashes` failed on BOTH hashes and
# read as "🔴 THE AUTHOR'S SCRIPT CHANGED … every 'line N' reference in this
# project now points at a different statement". The author's script had not
# changed at all; the checkout filter had. Both hashes match the LF form exactly.
#
# ⚠️ THAT IS THE WORST DIRECTION FOR THIS PARTICULAR RAIL TO FAIL IN. It exists to
# shout when a member's script is swapped under our line-number references, so a
# line-ending false positive teaches whoever sees it that the loudest alarm in the
# fixture directory cries wolf — and the remedy it invites (re-record the hashes)
# would bake this box's CRLF into a manifest every other checkout then fails.
#
# Same class as the note-connector fixtures below, same fix. Applies to all 510
# tracked `.pine` files, not just the member two: the corpus rosters, the probe
# integrity sweep and the linemaps all compare Pine bytes or characters.
*.pine text eol=lf

# note-connectors cross-language schema rail (Task 5): the Python drift test
# (`test_note_convert_fixtures.py`) byte-compares a freshly regenerated copy
# of these fixtures against the committed ones. `fixtures_gen.py` always
# writes `\n`-only. Without `eol=lf` here, `core.autocrlf=true` (this box) on
# a future clone/checkout would silently rewrite the committed copies to
# CRLF, and the drift test would then report every fixture as "stale" for a
# line-ending reason that has nothing to do with converter drift — the same
# CRLF-only-on-Windows failure class as the chart-parity harness above.
api/services/journal_two/note_connectors/convert/fixtures_in/*.md text eol=lf
api/services/journal_two/note_connectors/convert/fixtures_in/*.html text eol=lf
app/src/pages/journal-2-0/lib/importer/__fixtures__/server_convert/*.json text eol=lf
